{%- comment -%}
  HOP + LUXLIGHT + HOP subfamily (Ultra Repair / Colour Last / Smooth
  Hydration) editorial media parity fix.

  Contains no markup: scopes a shared frame treatment (rounded corners,
  contained 650:462-ratio media, official-measured column gap) to the
  editorial media/text sections of the HOP, LUXLIGHT and 3 HOP-subfamily
  range pages, by section id. Does not touch UNDER (its own dedicated
  montibello-under-layout.liquid already covers the same treatment there),
  product-card grids, PDPs, hero, header, footer, or any other page — those
  sections reuse the same component files (montibello-image-banner,
  montibello-feature-rows, montibello-stats-panel) with their own
  settings/IDs untouched.

  MANAGER FEEDBACK SPRINT (Perú vs España annotated review) extended this
  file's original selector list (HOP + Luxlight only) to also cover Ultra
  Repair / Colour Last / Smooth Hydration, which had never received this
  pass and were flagged for the exact same media-radius/spacing/heading-
  size gaps — reconciled into this one file rather than creating 3 more
  near-duplicate ones, per the task's "ONE source of truth" instruction.
  Also added at this pass: heading-size normalization (item B) and
  inter-row spacing (item D), both previously unaddressed in this file.

  Values below were measured live in-browser against the official
  reference (hair.montibello.com/gama/luxlight, /gama/hop, /gama/hop/hop-repair)
  today, not guessed:
    - editorial media: 650x462px @ 1440px viewport (aspect-ratio 650/462),
      border-radius 12px, object-fit: cover
    - 2-column container: max-width 1300px
    - visual gap from media edge to the text column's own content: ~48px
      (the official markup implements this as inner padding on the text
      column rather than a grid gap, but the rendered visual gap is the
      same either way, so it's applied here as column-gap for simplicity)
    - editorial H2/H3 heading size: 40px @ desktop (≥750px), 35px @ mobile,
      weight 700 — every heading on the official page (range title through
      every editorial row) renders at this exact uniform size; Peru's
      equivalent headings measured 48px, visibly larger, confirming the
      manager's "TÍTULO MÁS PEQUEÑO" notes
    - inter-row vertical gap: ~50px between one row's image and the next's
      on the official page; Peru's HOP page measured as little as 15px
      between its 2nd and 3rd editorial rows (image bottom to next image
      top) — applied here as a floor via padding-block-start on every row
      after the first
    - editorial background: rgb(246, 246, 243) on the official page
      (computed against <html>) vs Peru's plain white; applied here scoped
      to just these editorial rows, not globally
  Every affected section already uses `object-fit: cover` on its own
  image markup, so cropping behavior is unchanged — only the frame's
  size/radius changes, not what fills it.
{%- endcomment -%}

